204:### 2.8 Prompt-stack guide reflection / benchmark maintenance
205-
206-Use when:
207-- an attached guide, canon, or pattern document is the comparison target
208-- the task is to check whether actual prompt docs still reflect that governing source
209-- benchmark question generation, self Q/A, answer verification, and patch / rerun loops are the real work
--
221-- `PROMPT_tool_protocol_overlay` when OCR, MCP, or tool-mediated capability inspection materially changes evidence quality
222-- `PROMPT_guardrails_safety_overlay` when disclosure, mutation, or approval risk changes the benchmark path
223-
224-Typical packets:
225-- `Benchmark registry memo` for chapter-family inventory, cohort scope, or expected packet floor
226:- `Guide reflection benchmark memo` for question -> answer -> verification -> patch-target loops
227-- `Prompt-stack release review` when the benchmark is deciding release, rewrite acceptance, or parity preservation
228-- `Packet compliance report` when packet-floor doctrine or omission findings are the live surface
229-- `Context sufficiency review memo` or `Critique quality review memo` when weak context or no-gain iteration may explain benchmark instability
230-
231-Keep these maintenance control families direct in the runtime surface:
--
234-- document-benchmark to assembled-replay escalation
235-- route choice between staying document-grounded vs escalating to behavior proof
236-
237-Default route policy for this maintenance class:
238-- primary route: stay at document-level benchmark while the live question is doc/runtime parity, chapter-family answerability, or benchmark coverage
239:- fallback route: escalate to assembled replay when ambiguity, conflict, or behavior-critical claims need stronger evidence than document-grounded review can provide
240-- final ownership reroutes to `eval-ops` once the decision depends on replay execution state, benchmark gating, or release-sensitive continuation rather than route comparison alone
241-
242-Direct family note:
243-- for `runtime owner integrity` and `benchmark-loop adequacy`, document-level benchmark is the primary sufficient surface when runtime-owned docs directly expose the owner boundary or benchmark loop
244-- replay escalation is not required for those families unless the claim extends from document/runtime parity into assembled behavior proof or runner execution state
--
284-- A2A lifecycle-aware collaboration -> `A2A task-handoff memo`
285-- process-quality or replay-safe inspection -> `Safe trajectory artifact report`
286-- tool regression or deterministic harness evaluation -> `Mock-tool evaluation report`
287-- bounded multi-view challenge -> `Debate / consensus comparison memo`
288-- prompt-stack rewrite or release audit -> `Prompt-stack release review`
289:- guide-chapter reflection or doc-to-runtime parity benchmark -> `Guide reflection benchmark memo`
290-- assembled prompt replay setup -> `Benchmark cohort manifest`
291-- assembled prompt replay runner-state verdict -> `Replay runner verdict sheet`
292-- assembled prompt replay suite summary -> `Replay suite verdict memo`
293-- governance-owned packet-floor audit or omission-sensitive review -> `Packet compliance report`
294-- versioned replay suite or benchmark cohort definition -> `Benchmark registry memo`
--
332-- Retrieval / RAG -> `PROMPT_retrieval_grounding_overlay` + `grounded-research`; prefer `Evidence target / retrieval-mode memo` or `Source consultation ledger`
333-- Resource-Aware Optimization -> base prompts plus `PROMPT_search_reasoning_overlay`; prefer `Resource budget and route-choice memo`
334-- Reasoning Techniques / Reflection -> `PROMPT_search_reasoning_overlay`; prefer `Critique quality review memo` when critique utility or no-gain loops are under review
335-- Appendix A / advanced prompting execution families -> `PROMPT_search_reasoning_overlay` for decomposition, step-back, self-consistency, ReAct-like loops, tree-style search, and bounded reflection; keep prompt chaining in base prompts and treat example-catalog references as structure-only
336-- Guardrails / Safety -> `PROMPT_guardrails_safety_overlay`
337:- Evaluation / Monitoring -> `PROMPT_evaluation_monitoring_overlay` + `eval-ops`; prefer `Benchmark registry memo`, `Guide reflection benchmark memo`, or `Prompt-stack release review`
338-
339-Lookup rule:
340:- if a chapter family can only be answered by operator-facing prose and not by the active runtime / skill surface, treat that as a reflection gap and patch the actual prompt docs before claiming parity
341-
342-Packet rule:
343-- one packet should solve one control problem
344-- if packet overhead exceeds its decision value, simplify or drop it
345-- if a task family has a required packet floor, do not silently downgrade it to an optional convenience note
